{
  "delta_from_prior": "Replaces both the prior 18-var C7 fixture (peak 1 due to single-negative-occurrence DP cascades on branching) and Neon58's 20-var twin-pair product (108 clauses, 2-var XORs) with a 24-var, 264-clause twin-free hypergraph-transversal UNSAT family using 3-var XOR encodings (compressing 24->16 vars, 264->60 clauses, max width 8). Breaks Fable73's proposed link-twin contraction because every quotient vertex has a unique hyperedge incidence set while preserving neg>=2 across early branching layers.",
  "explanation": "### 1. Code Audit of Pinned v5 (`blq-composed-core-scc-emra-ialh5-v5`)\nAuditing all supplied files (`run_counting`, `compression.py`, `core_refutation.py`, `check_scc_and_growth.py`, `test_elim.py`, `test_mra.py`) finds **no soundness bug** producing a wrong SAT/UNSAT answer:\n- **Exact root compression (`compression.py`)**: `_verify_certificate` constructs `blocks` from every clause of `dense_formula(formula, ids)`, rejects duplicate literals, checks `sum(counts) == len(quotient)`, verifies every referenced `forms[i]` is supported inside its block's `support`, checks exact local truth-table equality `evaluate(clauses, x) == evaluate(q, image)` over all `2**|support|` local assignments, and checks `P * L = I` entrywise over GF(2). By conjunction over blocks and surjectivity of `P`, equisatisfiability is sound.\n- **Composed core refutation (`core_refutation.py` + `run_counting`)**: `probe` checks `set(core).issubset(set(f))` independently, compresses `core`, and only returns `UNSAT` when the compressed quotient is binary (`len(c) <= 2`) and refuted by `two_sat`. Composing `probe` once on the exact root quotient is sound by exact equisatisfiability; any `SAT`/`UNKNOWN`/budget failure falls back to exact residual search.\n- **Residual solver (`run_counting_core`, `canon_plus`, `elim_plus`, `refute`, `prune`)**: UP, subsumption, signed SCC collapsing, size-nonincreasing DP resolution, IALH-5 dual certificates verified in exact `Fraction` arithmetic, and syntactic subsumption pruning (`below(g, h)`) are all sound.\n\nNo correctness fixture is available; we therefore target **residual growth after clean, Lean-checkable scalable compression** on a larger 24-variable instance that also defeats Fable73's proposed nonlinear link-twin contraction.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Construction: 24-Variable Twin-Free Hypergraph-Transversal Fixture\nStart from a 16-variable quotient on two disjoint 8-variable sides:\n- **Side A** variables `{1, 9, 3, 11, 5, q13, 7, q15}` with 6 positive hyperedges:\n  $$\\mathcal{A} = \\{\\{1,9\\}, \\{3,11\\}, \\{5,q_{13}\\}, \\{7,q_{15}\\}, \\{1,3,5\\}, \\{9,11,7\\}\\}.$$\n- **Side B** variables `{2, 10, 4, 12, 6, q14, 8, q16}` with symmetric hyperedges:\n  $$\\mathcal{B} = \\{\\{2,10\\}, \\{4,12\\}, \\{6,q_{14}\\}, \\{8,q_{16}\\}, \\{2,4,6\\}, \\{10,12,8\\}\\}.$$\n\n**Twin-freeness (defeating Fable73 link-twin contraction)**: Unlike Neon58's disjoint pairs, adding the two 3-edges `{1,3,5}` and `{9,11,7}` breaks every twin pair: `1` is in `{1,9},{1,3,5}`, `9` in `{1,9},{9,11,7}`, `3` in `{3,11},{1,3,5}`, `11` in `{3,11},{9,11,7}`, `5` in `{5,q13},{1,3,5}`, `q13` only in `{5,q13}`, `7` in `{7,q15},{9,11,7}`, and `q15` only in `{7,q15}`. All 16 quotient variables have distinct positive-hyperedge neighborhoods.\n\n**Quotient clauses (60 clauses, 16 variables)**:\n1. **Side A negative clauses (12 width-4 clauses)**: The exact minimal hitting sets of $\\mathcal{A}$ \u2014 all 16 transversals of the 4 pairs except the 4 that miss a 3-edge (`{9,11,q13,7}`, `{9,11,q13,q15}`, `{1,3,5,q15}`, `{1,3,q13,q15}`).\n2. **Side B negative clauses (12 width-4 clauses)**: Symmetric minimal hitting sets of $\\mathcal{B}$.\n3. **Cross positive clauses (36 clauses)**: $A \\cup B$ for all $(A, B) \\in \\mathcal{A} \\times \\mathcal{B}$ (16 width-4, 16 width-5, 4 width-6).\n\n**UNSAT proof and nearby SAT control**:\n- Any assignment with no all-0 hyperedge in $\\mathcal{A}$ picks a 1 in each pair and in `{1,3,5}` and `{9,11,7}`; checking all 4 omitted transversals shows replacing one coordinate with a 1 from the missed 3-edge always hits one of the 12 negative clauses. Thus some $A \\in \\mathcal{A}$ is all-0, and symmetrically some $B \\in \\mathcal{B}$ is all-0, falsifying $A \\cup B$.\n- **Nearby SAT control**: Dropping any single cross clause $A \\cup B$ (e.g., `{1,3,5,2,4,6}`) makes the formula SAT by setting $A$ and $B$ to all-0 and all other variables to 1.\n\n**3-variable XOR lifting to 24 variables (264 clauses, 60 blocks)**:\nReplace the four low-degree variables with 3-variable parities:\n$$q_{13} = 13 \\oplus 14 \\oplus 15,\\quad q_{15} = 16 \\oplus 17 \\oplus 18,\\quad q_{14} = 19 \\oplus 20 \\oplus 21,\\quad q_{16} = 22 \\oplus 23 \\oplus 24.$$\nEach occurrence of `-q` expands to the 4 odd-parity clauses on its 3 variables; `+q` expands to the 4 even-parity clauses. This gives 60 Side-A clauses, 60 Side-B clauses, and 144 cross clauses (264 total), with max block width 8 (8 width-8 blocks, 8 width-7, 24 width-6, 8 width-5, 12 width-4), total local points `5056 <= 16384`, and verification work well below `8,000,000`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Expected Behavior on Pinned v5\n1. **Clean root compression (24 -> 16 vars, 264 -> 60 clauses)**:\n   Block frequencies of the 16 independent forms are: `5, 6, 7, 8` (19 blocks), `1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11, 12` (18 blocks), and the four 3-var XORs (11 blocks). All linear combinations of `{1..12}` (e.g. `1^3`) are skipped as dependent once `{1..12}` are chosen; combinations mixing a singleton with a 3-var XOR appear in at most 6 blocks (`< 11`). Thus `compress_root` selects the exact 16-form adapted basis, verifies the local-table + GF(2) right-inverse certificate, and is eligible for Lean verification.\n2. **Core refutation UNKNOWN at both stages**:\n   On the original 264-clause input, every block is a single affine coset of its stabilizer (size 1, 4, or 16), so `counts[v] == 0` for all $v$ outside the stabilizer; `probe` removes 0 clauses (`no_clauses_removed`). On the 60-clause quotient, every block has size 1, so `probe` again returns `UNKNOWN (no_clauses_removed)`.\n3. **Residual branching growth (peak >= 8, distinct from discovery failure)**:\n   Ascending quotient order branches on `5, 6, 7, 8` first (one variable from each of four pairs across both sides), then `1, 2, 3, 4`. At the root and through layers 1\u20133 (`5, 6, 7`), every window of size `<= 5` has a full-dimensional integer affine hull (so IALH-5 returns `UNKNOWN`), no 2-SAT SCC exists, and unlike our prior 18-var $C_7$ fixture (which collapsed to peak 1 via single-negative-occurrence DP cascades), every active variable maintains `neg >= 2` across layers 1\u20132 and avoids UNSAT cascades across all 8 branches of layer 3, yielding 8 incomparable residual states at depth 3 (peak >= 8) while keeping width-5/6 cross clauses sparse for IALH-5 runtime control.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Critique of Fable's Nonlinear Proposals\nFable73's link-twin contraction relies on exact neighborhood equivalence of paired literals, which fails immediately on this twin-free hypergraph family without needing large clause counts. More generally, any local nonlinear gadget contraction (or fibre-transfer/collapse-rank rule) faces a structural obstruction: without a sound, polynomially checkable global invariant over arbitrary hypergraph transversals, deleting any single cross clause flips UNSAT to SAT while leaving local 5-variable windows unchanged.",
